'''''Bavaricarbo''''' is an extinct genus of [[cormorant]] (family Phalacrocoracidae) from the [[Miocene]] [[Hammerschmiede clay pit]], Germany. The type and only species is '''''B. brevirostris'''''.<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Mayr |first1=Gerald |last2=Lechner |first2=Thomas |last3=Böhme |first3=Madelaine |date=2026-09-10 |title=A new short-beaked stem group cormorant (Phalacrocoracidae), an unusual new hawk (Accipitridae), a small swift (Apodidae), and other avian remains from the early Late Miocene hominid Fossil-Lagerstätte Hammerschmiede, southern Germany |url=https://sjp.pensoft.net/article/200204/ |journal=Swiss Journal of Palaeontology |language=en |publisher=Pensoft Publishers |volume=145 |pages=927–941 |doi=10.3897/sjp.145.200204 |doi-access=free |issn=1664-2384}}</ref>

